  "about": "FM1VST's cores (CORES-PLAN.md; branch cores-all 2026-10-18, the pins and LOOM-8 2026-10-21; DUELL un-gated, Mini-Tone, FMini-1, Skiff, GR!MM, PIGEON, Tonitor and Speak37 2026-10-22; LOOM-8 0.6.1, DUELL 1.0, CoralFlower 0.5 and Tonitor 0.55 the same day, branch bump-oct23): the firmware each core builds, at FM1VST's pinned version, its licence (CORES-PLAN section 1), the browser's category / tag / author (FM1VST plugin/Sheet.cpp FirmwareMeta), and the licensing gate (section 6). Only the un-gated twenty-one are built for the web and hosted (native; ChoralRoot and Melodee un-gated 2026-10-19: their CZ-1 and Prophet-5 presets ship compiled into the firmware, no raw .syx is published; LOOM-8 un-gated 2026-10-21, its factory 909 hi-hat unchanged, the owner's call); every Hub firmware also runs emulated, fetched from where the Hub points at play time. An un-gated core the Hub does not list (LOOM-8, Speak37's FM-1 build; Mini-Tone and FMini-1 until the snapshot has them) is native only, from these fields: name, what, release, authorFull. nativeName: the name the native build goes by (DUELL's, as FM1VST names it: its naming terms for unofficial builds). hubVersion: the Hub's name for the version the core builds (Tonitor). nativeDefault: why the native core stays the default though the Hub's version is newer (live.js newestWins). hub: the Hub's id where it differs from FM1VST's core id. glue / commit / repo: the core-glue folder, the submodule commit FM1VST pins and its URL (the native source link), and fm1vst: FM1VST's own commit; build_catalog.mjs reads all of them from web/vendor/FM1VST and uses these only when it is not checked out.",
